Independent FX.25 fixtures
=========================
Dire Wolf revision: eda1383f5fa9d8ba3cb27f99db1d2c79494404c9 (GPL-2.0-or-later).
Reproduce: see docs/fx25.md and scripts/fx25/interop.py.

direwolf.json: 33 raw wire vectors (11 standard tags, short/boundary/maximum
frames), generated by unmodified Dire Wolf fx25_send_frame through reference.c.
Includes literal 7e/ff/00 tails, real FCS/stuffing, and shortened RS parity.

direwolf.wav: 33 clean mono recordings from real Dire Wolf gen_packets;
short, boundary and near-maximum text payloads for every standard tag.

direwolf-damaged.wav: 11 recordings, using the reference wire encoder and
unmodified Dire Wolf gen_tone.c via modulate.c. Exactly parity/2 data symbols
are XOR-corrupted before modulation. Plain HDLC cannot decode them. Expected
payloads are independent inputs recorded in direwolf.json (damaged_frames).

All recordings are synthetic offline fixtures; no RF performance claim.
SHA256SUMS records the checked-in fixture checksums. The interoperability
script additionally requires Graywolf-generated audio to decode byte-exactly
ONCE with real Dire Wolf atest (-L 1 -G 1 -h), for each of the 33 wire vectors.
